---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/observatory.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Brambley Observatory" description="Observations from the edge of the Olympic lowlands." bodyClass="observatory-page-body">
<!-- Brambley Observatory landing page. Styles are embedded below for page isolation. -->
<div class="brambley-observatory" id="brambley-observatory">

  <!-- Compact photographic hero -->
  <section class="bo-hero" aria-labelledby="bo-title">
    <img class="bo-hero-image"
      src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/6924ab5c9e143a2b135919b8/73c3d739-8806-4964-a3f3-83e21af060e5/IMG_0698.JPEG?content-type=image%2Fjpeg"
      alt="Snow-covered landscape at Brambley"
      fetchpriority="high">
    <div class="bo-hero-shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <nav class="bo-nav" aria-label="Brambley navigation">
      <a href="/home">HOME</a>
      <a href="/blog">NOTES</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="bo-hero-content bo-container">
      <div class="bo-eyebrow">GRAYS HARBOR · WASHINGTON</div>
      <h1 id="bo-title"><span>BRAMBLEY</span> <span>OBSERVATORY</span></h1>
      <p class="bo-hero-subtitle">Observations from the edge of the Olympic lowlands</p>
      <div class="bo-hero-topics">
        <span>WEATHER</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span>SEISMOLOGY</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span>NATURAL PHENOMENA</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <a class="bo-scroll" href="#observatory-instruments" aria-label="Explore the instruments">
      <span>EXPLORE</span><b aria-hidden="true">↓</b>
    </a>
  </section>

  <!-- Instruments immediately follow the hero -->
  <section class="bo-instruments" id="observatory-instruments" aria-labelledby="bo-instruments-title">
    <div class="bo-container">
      <div class="bo-section-heading">
        <div class="bo-section-label light"><span>THE INSTRUMENTS</span></div>
        <h2 id="bo-instruments-title">Continuous observations from Brambley.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="bo-card-grid">
        <article class="bo-card" aria-labelledby="bo-weather-title">
          <a href="/wxstation" class="bo-card-image bo-weather-image" aria-label="Visit the weather station">
            <img
              src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/6924ab5c9e143a2b135919b8/4a5f58da-4c7c-4d99-a98b-f749c6bef5a1/IMG_9989.JPG?content-type=image%2Fjpeg"
              alt="Clouds over the pond at Brambley" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div class="bo-card-image-shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <span class="bo-card-tag">METEOROLOGY</span>
          </a>
          <div class="bo-card-body">
            <h3 id="bo-weather-title">Weather Station</h3>
            <p>Continuous observations of temperature, humidity, atmospheric pressure,
              precipitation, wind, solar radiation and other conditions at Brambley.</p>
            <div class="bo-card-links">
              <a href="/wxstation"><span>LIVE OBSERVATIONS</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b></a>
              <a href="/weather-data-archive"><span>WEATHER ARCHIVE</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b></a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="bo-card" aria-labelledby="bo-seismic-title">
          <a href="/seismic" class="bo-card-image bo-seismic-image" aria-label="Visit the seismic station">
            <!-- The source image stays intact. CSS crops it inside the card so the
                 main earthquake trace runs through the lower quarter. -->
            <img class="bo-seismic-source"
              src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/6924ab5c9e143a2b135919b8/1205586c-222c-4af3-a340-bc54ec08c438/IMG_6719.PNG?content-type=image%2Fpng"
              alt="Earthquake waveform recorded at Brambley"
              width="946" height="2048" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <span class="bo-card-tag">SEISMOLOGY</span>
          </a>
          <div class="bo-card-body">
            <h3 id="bo-seismic-title">Seismic Station</h3>
            <p>A Raspberry Shake seismometer continuously records ground motion at
              Brambley, capturing earthquakes from the Pacific Northwest and,
              occasionally, much farther away.</p>
            <div class="bo-card-links">
              <a href="/seismic"><span>LIVE SEISMOMETER</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b></a>
              <a href="/quakearchive"><span>EARTHQUAKE ARCHIVE</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b></a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The personal story follows the instrument destinations -->
  <section class="bo-intro" id="why-observe" aria-labelledby="bo-story-title">
    <div class="bo-intro-inner bo-container">
      <div class="bo-section-label"><span>WHY OBSERVE?</span></div>
      <h2 id="bo-story-title">A few more data points in a very long record.</h2>
      <div class="bo-intro-copy">
        <p>Many years ago, I was walking on the Scripps Pier in La Jolla when I
          read the story of oceanographer George McEwen. Beginning in the early
          twentieth century, McEwen kept handwritten records of ocean temperature
          and salinity off the pier. At the time, he was one of very few people
          making such observations along the Pacific Rim. Today, the data he
          collected is vital to our understanding of how the ocean is evolving.</p>
        <p>The story inspired me to think about what data I could record and
          preserve that might one day prove valuable to our understanding of how
          the Pacific Northwest is changing over time. Where could I add data
          points to areas of scientific research?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Compact Field Observations section; no metadata line -->
  <section class="bo-field" aria-labelledby="bo-field-title">
    <div class="bo-field-image">
      <img
        src="https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/6924ab5c9e143a2b135919b8/566dd344-1a22-4efe-8dd6-29b17c6c3c54/IMG_0680.JPG?content-type=image%2Fjpeg"
        alt="Atmospheric optical phenomenon observed at Brambley" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </div>
    <div class="bo-field-content">
      <div class="bo-section-label"><span>FIELD OBSERVATIONS</span></div>
      <h2 id="bo-field-title">Beyond the<br>instruments.</h2>
      <p>Instruments tell only part of the story. Field Observations will collect
        less formal records from around Brambley: unusual weather and atmospheric
        phenomena, seasonal changes, astronomical events, and other occurrences
        worth noting as the landscape changes over time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="bo-footer">
    <div class="bo-footer-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="bo-footer-location">GRAYS HARBOR, WASHINGTON · 47° N</div>
  </footer>
</div>
</BaseLayout>